commit 1391672cbb1f672a8cd2d0f6842167c1114da36e
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 02:00:40 2026 +0200

    pretrain: run L2-ES to the 1.7B reference
    
    ES was capped at the 1B rung on 2026-09-10 because Spanish is the thinnest
    L2 source: the build realizes 23.9B, so the 1.7B's 83.6B draw is 3.51
    epochs, against Russian's 1.15 and Chinese's 1.61. Uncapped because that
    repetition stays under the ~4 epochs at which repeated tokens stop being
    worth close to fresh ones, so the score a decision reads should land where
    a less-repeated run would — and because the cell is what makes the
    second-language axis reportable at all: with A, ZH and ES at the reference,
    `lang2` goes from one mono-axis pair to the three rule 5 needs. Measured,
    not assumed: every other axis is unmoved (L 39, arch 10, list 6, T 4).
    Grid 185 -> 186 runs.
    
    The three epoch counts are not comparable, and that is the cost, so the
    registry comment, both READMEs and the training plan all record 3.51x.
    
    Nothing warned about this. `undersized_build` asks whether a build is
    smaller than its SOURCE could give, and ES exhausts every Spanish token
    there is, so the cell passed in silence — an `allow_undersized` entry would
    have been dead registry state, and would have masked the refusal if ES were
    ever rebuilt short of its source. `fineweb_epochs` answers the other
    question instead, and the launcher prints `repeats its multilingual half
    N.NNx` for any L>1 cell drawing more than one epoch.
    
    Verified: fineweb_source returns short=None for ES at 1.7B (3.51 epochs)
    while ZH's refusal is unchanged (1.61 epochs from a 52.0B build);
    `--scheme ES --dry-run` shows the cell live, not blocked; check_rules 0
    findings; sync_docs and sync_models_json both report no change.

